[Intro]

[Verse 1]
[00:11.28]Lay him down where the rowans bend
[00:17.27]Lay him down where the stones do keep
[00:23.68]Cover his eyes with the soft white moss
[00:29.89]Cover his hands with the winter's sleep

[00:37.69]Bring no fire, bring no flame
[00:40.48]Bring the silence the night doth bring
[00:43.62]Speak no name, for the name is gone
[00:46.76]Only the wind shall remember him

[Chorus]
[00:52.19]Heyr oss, Skogarmóðir
[00:58.13]Take him gently to thy breast
[01:04.20]Vér leggjum hann niðr
[01:09.82]In the cairn of wintering rest

[Verse 2]
[01:17.33]He was the hand upon the plough
[01:23.08]He was the song at the longhouse door
[01:29.29]He was the breath of a quiet hearth
[01:34.42]He shall be these things no more

[01:41.08]Sister-snow, she shroudeth him
[01:44.14]Brother-stone, he keepeth watch
[01:47.13]Mother-root, she gathereth him
[01:50.22]Down into the dark and soft

[Chorus]
[01:55.77]Heyr oss, Skogarmóðir
[02:01.80]Take him gently to thy breast
[02:08.12]Vér leggjum hann niðr
[02:13.39]In the cairn of wintering rest

[Bridge]
[02:20.34]And we who stand, and we who stay
[02:23.47]We shall walk a shorter road
[02:26.48]We shall carry a heavier coat
[02:29.57]We shall sing a quieter song

[Final verse]
[02:40.70]Lay him down where the rowans bend
[02:46.66]Lay him down where the stones do keep
[02:53.06]Cover his eyes with the soft white moss
[02:58.98]Cover his hands with the winter's sleep

[Outro]
